kikhawmin = (t:v) (w:gather/assemble/come together) (d:kikhawm with the linking ending -in: gathering, having assembled) (e:Israel upate ~ Ramah-a Samuel kiangah) (b:kikhawm) (r:9.8.4/9.17.2) (q:draft)
kiphawk = (t:v) (w:be remembered/be missed) (d:passive of phawk; with nawn lo, be forgotten) (e:amah ~ tawntung ding hi) (b:phawk) (r:19.112.6/9.20.18) (q:draft)
kisaktheihpih = (t:v) (w:boast of/be proud of/take pride in) (d:be proud on account of something, such as wealth or strength) (e:na hauhna na ~ hi) (b:kisaktheih) (r:26.28.5/19.49.6) (q:draft)
kulhpite = (t:n) (w:walls/strongholds/fortresses) (e:Jerusalem ~ ciang kik in) (b:kulhpi) (r:19.51.18/26.19.7) (q:draft)
luangsak = (t:v) (w:cause to flow/make flow/shed) (d:luang flow with the causative sak; sisan luangsak is shed blood) (e:gunte bangin tuite ~ hi) (b:luang) (r:19.78.16/13.28.3) (q:draft)
