damna = (t:n) (w:healing/cure/recovery) (d:dam with the ending -na; damna ngah is be healed) (e:Mi sawmte in ~ ngah hilo ahi hiam) (b:dam) (r:42.17.17/24.46.11) (q:draft)
halin = (t:v) (w:burn/set on fire) (d:hal burn with the linking ending in, used when another action follows in the same sentence) (e:Pasian’ inn ~ Jerusalem kulh nusia uh) (b:hal) (r:14.36.19/11.11.8) (q:draft)
hoi = (t:v) (w:stagger/reel/lean/totter) (d:to sway or lean over as if about to fall, like a drunk person or a leaning wall) (e:Leitung pumpi zukham bangin ~ ding a) (r:23.24.20/18.12.25) (q:draft)
