luanghawmte = (t:n) (w:dead bodies/corpses/carcasses) (e:a site’ ~ ka pia ding hi) (b:luanghawm) (r:9.17.46/13.10.12) (q:draft)
maan = (t:adj) (w:true/honest/right/just) (d:correct and without falsehood, said of scales, words and offerings; usually a maan before the noun) (e:A ~ tawikhaina leh tawitehnate) (r:20.16.11/20.8.7) (q:draft)
maan = (t:v) (w:reign/rule) (d:to be king; in the verses written maan’ with an apostrophe, before laitakin for during the reign of, or before zawh, as in a maan’ zawh kum li the fourth year of his reign) (e:Zedekiah a ~’ zawh kum sawm) (r:24.39.2/24.26.18) (q:draft)
ngatin = (t:v) (w:face/turn toward) (d:ngat with the linking ending in, with the face or ear turned toward something while another action follows) (e:a mai kawm lam ~ Topa tungah thungen) (b:ngat) (r:12.20.2/1.42.6) (q:draft)
nidangin = (t:adv) (w:formerly/in the past/before) (e:~ a kiho thei kei uh hi) (b:nidang) (r:42.23.12/57.1.11) (q:draft)
nupite = (t:n) (w:women) (d:plural of nupi, grown or married women) (e:~ leh naupangte a muh ciangin) (b:nupi) (r:1.33.5/19.68.12) (q:draft)
pauna = (t:n) (w:speech/words/speaking) (d:what a person says, or the act of speaking; pau with na) (e:~ leh kammal om lo a) (b:pau) (r:19.19.3/18.15.6) (q:draft)
phah = (t:v) (w:spread/lay out) (d:to spread cloth, a covering or a table flat over something) (e:lampi-ah puante a ~ uh hi) (r:42.19.36/19.78.19) (q:draft)
phatin = (t:v) (w:praise/give thanks) (d:phat with the linking ending in, praising or thanking while another action follows) (e:Pasian’ min ~ biakna innpi sungah) (b:phat) (r:42.24.53/13.23.30) (q:draft)
sakhat = (t:n) (w:one flesh/one piece) (d:sa flesh and khat one; a single body, said of husband and wife and of things made in one piece with another) (e:amaute in ~ suak uh hi) (r:1.2.24/2.25.36) (q:draft)
thuaknate = (t:n) (w:sufferings/afflictions) (e:amau’ ~ ka lunghimawh a) (b:thuakna) (r:2.3.7/19.25.18) (q:draft)
thuciamnate = (t:n) (w:promises/vows) (d:plural of thuciamna; God's promises or the vows a person has made) (e:na ~ na tungsak ding hi) (b:thuciamna) (r:18.22.27/19.119.140) (q:draft)
tuinak = (t:n) (w:spring/fountain) (d:a place where water comes out of the ground) (e:nuntakna ~ tawh kibang a) (r:20.14.27/14.32.4) (q:draft)
bua = (t:v) (w:pour out/shed/spill) (d:to pour out a liquid, also of rain falling, blood being shed and the Spirit being poured out) (e:ka Kha ka ~ ding hi) (r:29.2.29/66.16.6) (q:draft)
bulah = (t:n) (w:at the base/at the foot/at the bottom) (d:bul base with the place marker ah) (e:biakna tau ~ a sisan sung khia hi) (b:bul) (r:3.9.9/3.4.30) (q:draft)
cithak = (t:n) (w:sore/scall/itch) (d:an itching or festering disease of the skin, in the laws about skin diseases) (e:a ~ in a vun sung a lawh) (r:3.13.35/3.21.20) (q:draft)
dawnna = (t:n) (w:drinking/drink) (d:the act of drinking, from dawn drink; dawnna hai is a drinking cup) (e:leenggahtui thak ~ in nungakte thadimsak ding) (b:dawn) (r:38.9.17/45.14.21) (q:draft)
dawnna = (t:n) (w:meeting/place of meeting) (d:the act or place of going to meet someone, from dawn meet, welcome) (e:Martha’ ~ munah a om lai hi) (b:dawn) (r:43.11.30) (q:draft, low confidence)
dona = (t:n) (w:fighting/war/warfare/attack) (d:the act of fighting against someone, often as gal dona warfare) (e:gal ~ a theihtheih nading) (b:do) (r:7.3.2/10.11.7) (q:draft)
gamdangte = (t:n) (w:nations/foreign nations/foreign lands) (d:plural of gamdang; other countries and their peoples) (e:~ in a zu a dawn manun) (b:gamdang) (r:24.51.7/24.46.1) (q:draft)
gingsak = (t:v) (w:sound/make sound/cause to resound) (d:ging sound with sak, to make something sound out, such as a voice, a trumpet or an alarm) (e:Beth-aven khua-ah pataukohna ~ un) (b:ging) (r:28.5.8/10.22.14) (q:draft)
guahtui = (t:n) (w:rain/rainwater/shower) (d:guah rain and tui water) (e:~ tawh na nipsak a) (r:19.65.10/18.36.27) (q:draft)
gutate = (t:n) (w:thieves/robbers) (e:~ in ka biakinn luhin ninsak ding uh) (b:guta) (r:26.7.22/18.30.5) (q:draft)
halna = (t:n) (w:burning) (d:the act or place of burning, mostly in paknamtui halna the burning of incense) (e:paknamtui ~ leh tuidawn biakna) (b:hal) (r:24.44.18/14.29.7) (q:draft)
hansuah = (t:v) (w:stir up/urge/encourage/exhort) (d:to move people to act by words, for good or for bad) (e:siampi liante in mihonpi a ~ uh hi) (r:41.15.11/44.20.2) (q:draft)
hawl = (t:v) (w:drive/drive out/drive away) (d:to make people, animals or a vehicle move on; with khia drive out, with kik drive back) (e:Anak suan-le-khakte ~ khia hi) (r:6.15.14/2.14.25) (q:draft)
hawmsak = (t:v) (w:distribute/divide among/share out) (d:hawm with sak, to divide something and give it out to others) (e:a tute lakah a ~ hi) (b:hawm) (r:43.6.11/46.12.11) (q:draft)
kawlsing = (t:n) (c:plant) (w:pomegranate) (d:used in the name mang kawlsing, the pomegranate tree and its fruit) (e:mang ~ gah khat) (r:2.39.26/22.4.13) (q:draft)
khualzinna = (t:n) (w:journey/travel) (e:Jakob in a ~ zom a) (b:khualzin) (r:1.29.1/1.24.21) (q:draft)
khuasunga = (t:n) (w:in the city/in the town) (d:khuasung town with the ending a, in or of the town; mostly before om, as in Jerusalem khuasunga om those living in Jerusalem) (e:Tua ~ om mite pawl nih pha uh a) (b:khuasung) (r:44.14.4/44.4.16) (q:draft)
kidimin = (t:v) (w:be filled/be full) (d:kidim with the linking ending in, being full of or filled with something) (e:Kha Siangtho tawh ~ om un) (b:kidim) (r:49.5.18/44.6.8) (q:draft)
kihih = (t:v) (w:be done) (d:passive form with ki of hih do; something is done, or is done to someone) (e:Israelte sungah tua bang ~ lo hi) (r:10.13.12/9.17.27) (q:draft)
kiling = (t:v) (w:be shaken/be moved/shake) (d:to be made to shake or lose firmness, of the earth, a building or a person) (e:ka ~ kei ding hi) (r:19.16.8/19.96.10) (q:draft)
kisaktheihna = (t:n) (w:pride/boasting/conceit) (d:thinking too highly of oneself and showing it) (e:~ in siatna hong tuak sak a) (b:kisaktheih) (r:20.16.18/46.5.6) (q:draft)
kisat = (t:v) (w:be beaten/be struck/be battered) (d:passive form with ki of sat beat; also said of the heart pounding) (e:kongpite ~ khamin kisia hi) (b:sat) (r:23.24.12/23.1.5) (q:draft)
kitawng = (t:v) (w:quarrel/strive/fight) (d:to dispute or fight with one another) (e:Lampi-ah ~ kei un) (r:1.45.24/1.13.7) (q:draft)
kopin = (t:adv) (w:together/jointly/in pairs) (d:kop pair with in; joined with another, two together) (e:tua numei tawh ~ a nasemte in) (b:kop) (r:9.28.23/1.7.9) (q:draft)
kopin = (t:adv) (w:twined/doubled) (d:of thread twisted two together, in a kopin a kikhuk puan, where the English has finely twisted linen) (e:a ~ a kikhuk a kigan puan hoih) (b:kop) (r:2.38.16/2.35.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
kuangdai = (t:n) (w:plate/dish/platter) (d:a wide shallow dish, larger than kuang bowl) (e:shekel za leh sawmthum a gik ngun ~ khat) (r:4.7.13/4.7.84) (q:draft)
laikhak = (t:n) (w:letter) (d:a written message sent to someone) (e:a kamtaipa in ~ khat hong pia hi) (r:16.6.5/24.29.29) (q:draft)
laikhak = (t:v) (w:send a letter/write to) (e:kumpi Darias’ tungah ~ uh hi) (r:15.5.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
lamenin = (t:v) (w:hope/expect/wait for) (d:lamen with the linking ending in, hoping or expecting while another action follows) (e:a ngah ding ~ sawltakte a ento hi) (b:lamen) (r:44.3.5/45.8.19) (q:draft)
lampangah = (t:n) (w:on the side/at the side) (d:lampang side with the place marker ah; with a direction word, on the south side, on the north side) (e:biakbuk leitaw ~ giahphual sat ding uh a) (b:lampang) (r:4.3.29/9.20.20) (q:draft)
letmat = (t:n) (w:inch) (d:a small unit of length in the 1932 text, which gives cubits as pi feet and letmat; letmat kua, nine, stands for a span and pi nih le letmat thum for a cubit and a half) (e:a vai pi nih le ~ thum ciat ahi hi) (r:2.36.21/2.28.16) (q:draft, low confidence)
luanna = (t:n) (w:flowing/flow) (d:the flowing of a liquid such as tears or blood, or the place where it flows, as in the land flowing with milk and honey) (e:ka khitui ~ hong mu-in) (b:luan) (r:18.16.20/2.33.3) (q:draft)
neh = (t:v) (w:press hard/close in on/come near) (d:to push forward against someone or come up close, of an enemy, a battle or a crowd) (e:galte in amaute ~ mahmah uh hi) (r:9.13.6/9.31.3) (q:draft)
neh = (t:v) (w:prevail/win) (d:to gain the upper hand in a fight, likely the same word as press hard) (e:peuhmah ciangin Israel in ~ hi) (r:2.17.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
phawkkik = (t:v) (w:remember/recall) (d:phawk with kik again, to call back to mind; with sak, to remind) (e:a nungzuite in ~ uh a) (b:phawk) (r:43.2.22/19.25.6) (q:draft)
phuah = (t:v) (w:name/give a name) (d:to make up and give a new name, used with min name) (e:a min thak a ~ Piter) (r:41.3.16/12.17.34) (q:draft)
phuah = (t:v) (w:compose/make up/invent) (d:to compose a song, used with la song; also to invent a custom or a lie) (e:David bangin la ~ nuam na sa uh a) (r:30.6.5/26.26.17) (q:draft)
piakhia = (t:v) (w:give out/give away/give up/hand over) (d:pia give with khia out) (e:sihna dongin a nuntakna ~ a) (b:pia) (r:23.53.12/20.21.26) (q:draft)
seek = (t:v) (w:hammer/forge/beat) (d:to shape or sharpen metal by beating it) (e:Lo khawhna tuute namsau-in ~ un la) (r:29.3.10/4.16.39) (q:draft)
simmawhbawl = (t:v) (w:treat with contempt/despise/mock) (e:thuhilhnate ~ kei un) (b:simmawh) (r:52.5.20/45.14.3) (q:draft)
sumbukte = (t:n) (w:merchants/traders) (e:~ tungah tuate zuak hi) (b:sumbuk) (r:20.31.24/66.18.11) (q:draft)
taangin = (t:prep) (w:in place of/instead of/on behalf of) (d:follows the noun or pronoun it relates to; in someone's position, as a successor, substitute or representative) (e:a tapa Jehoshafat in ama ~ uk a) (r:14.17.1/11.2.35) (q:draft)
thuakte = (t:n) (w:those who suffer/the afflicted/the oppressed) (d:thuak suffer, bear with plural te; people who undergo hardship or oppression) (e:a ~ mangngilh kei in) (b:thuak) (r:19.10.12/19.9.9) (q:draft)
thukna = (t:n) (w:depth/the deep/depths) (d:a deep place, of the sea or a pit, from thuk deep) (e:a ~ sungah amaute kiasuk uh hi) (r:2.15.5/19.88.6) (q:draft)
thukna = (t:n) (w:revenge/vengeance/repayment) (d:the act of paying back, a wrong with revenge or a gift or kindness with something in return; heh thukna is vengeance in anger) (e:Heh ~ a muh ciangin) (b:thuk) (r:19.58.10/20.6.34) (q:draft)
zawk = (t:adv) (w:more) (d:form of zaw used after a descriptive word or verb when leh, ding, nading or kei follows; more, to a greater degree, as in a thuk zawk deeper) (e:kawm maitang sangin a thuk ~ tuak leh) (b:zaw) (r:3.14.37/42.13.2) (q:draft)
zongte = (t:n) (w:those who seek/seekers) (d:zong seek with plural te; the people who look for or try to get someone or something) (e:nangmah hong ~ nusia lo na hih manin) (r:19.9.10/19.70.4) (q:draft)
bawnghonte = (t:n) (w:herds/herds of cattle) (e:na ~ hoih takin kem in) (b:bawnghon) (r:20.27.23/2.12.32) (q:draft)
bukah = (t:n) (w:in the tent/to the tent/at the tabernacle) (d:buk tent, hut with the place marker ah; mostly in kikhopna bukah at the tent of meeting) (e:kikhopna ~ nasem dingin Levi mite pai ding) (r:4.8.15/3.4.16) (q:draft)
bulpite = (t:n) (w:foundations/bases) (e:mual ~ zong lingin kising damdam hi) (b:bulpi) (r:19.18.7/19.11.3) (q:draft)
denglum = (t:v) (w:stone to death/strike dead) (d:to kill by throwing or hurling something at a person or animal; with suang tawh, stone to death) (e:suang tawh amah ~ ding uh hi) (r:5.22.21/19.78.48) (q:draft)
encik = (t:v) (w:watch closely/keep an eye on) (d:to keep looking at someone carefully, to guard or to find fault) (e:a kipanin Saul in David ~ hi) (r:9.18.9/18.33.11) (q:draft)
galhangte = (t:n) (w:warriors/brave men/mighty men) (e:~ huhna ngenin kiko uh a) (b:galhang) (r:23.33.7/24.48.14) (q:draft)
galmatin = (t:adv) (w:as captives/captive/into captivity) (d:galmat captive with in; in the state of a prisoner of war, with verbs of carrying off or being) (e:i zite ~ om uh hi) (r:14.29.9/14.28.17) (q:draft)
gampa = (t:n) (w:wilderness/deserted place/lonely place) (d:uninhabited country; in the verses always as gampa lakah, in or into the wilderness) (e:Zeisu ~ lakah a sawl pah hi) (r:41.1.12/43.6.49) (q:draft)
hawlkhiatna = (t:n) (w:driving out/expulsion/banishment) (d:the act of driving people out, or with gam the land to which they were driven) (e:eite hong ~ gam khempeuh pana) (b:hawlkhiat) (r:24.16.15/5.9.4) (q:draft)
hihsak = (t:v) (w:do for/do to) (d:hih do with sak, to do something for or to another person; with lo, not let someone act against another) (e:eite’ adingin bang hong ~ thei lel ding) (r:28.10.3/10.21.3) (q:draft)
hingsak = (t:v) (w:make alive/give life/preserve/sustain) (d:hing alive with sak, to cause to live or keep alive; with kik, bring back to life) (e:na thu omsa bangin kei hong ~ in) (b:hing) (r:19.119.25/43.5.21) (q:draft)
khek = (t:v) (w:change/exchange/substitute) (d:to put one thing in the place of another, as clothes, skin or an animal for offering) (e:a puan a ~ khit ciangin) (r:1.41.14/24.13.23) (q:draft)
khuacingte = (t:n) (w:garrison/outpost/watchmen/guards) (d:plural of khuacing, those who guard a town; a body of soldiers stationed in a place) (e:Efraim khuapite sungah ~ koih hi) (r:14.17.2/22.5.7) (q:draft)
khuampeekte = (t:n) (w:frames/boards) (d:the upright wooden planks that form the walls of the tabernacle) (e:Biakbuk ~ na bawl ding hi) (b:khuampeek) (r:2.26.18/2.26.15) (q:draft)
kipahtawi = (t:v) (w:be exalted/be honored/be lifted high) (d:passive form with ki of pahtawi honor, exalt) (e:na hatna hangin nang hong ~ ta hen) (b:pahtawi) (r:19.21.13/19.12.8) (q:draft)
kulhte = (t:n) (w:walls/fortifications) (d:plural of kulh, the defensive walls of a city) (e:Na ~ sungah lungnopna om hen la) (b:kulh) (r:19.122.7/19.89.40) (q:draft)
lehhek = (t:v) (w:betray/deceive) (d:hand someone over treacherously or deal falsely with him; a lehhek pa is the betrayer) (e:amah a ~ pa in gimna thuak ding) (r:42.22.22/20.14.25) (q:draft)
liamna = (t:n) (w:wound/injury/sore) (e:ama ~ hangin damna i ngah hi) (b:liam) (r:23.53.5/2.21.25) (q:draft)
mawhte = (t:n) (w:sinners/wrongdoers/the guilty) (d:those who sin or do wrong; hong mawhte are those who wrong us, our debtors; numei tawh a mawhte, those who sin with women, are the sexually immoral) (e:Mi ~ angvanin diksak ding hoih lo) (b:mawh) (r:20.18.5/40.6.12) (q:draft)
meigongnu = (t:n) (w:widow) (d:a woman whose husband has died; nu marks a woman) (e:~ ka hi kei hi) (b:meigong) (r:66.18.7/54.5.9) (q:draft)
milip = (t:pron) (w:each one/everyone/every man) (d:each person individually, usually as a milip-in, each of them) (e:a ~-in a van uh suah uh hi) (r:1.44.11/2.32.27) (q:draft)
mitah = (t:n) (w:in the eyes/in the sight/on the eyes) (d:mit eye with the place marker ah; after Topa it means in the sight of the Lord) (e:Topa’ ~ a man gamta lo a) (b:mit) (r:14.28.1/43.9.11) (q:draft)
nun = (t:n) (w:bud/knob) (d:in the verses a bud-shaped ornament of the lampstand, named together with pak flower) (e:a ~ leh a pak tawh a om) (r:2.37.20/2.25.35) (q:draft)
nun = (t:v) (w:blow) (d:of wind or storm; written nun’ before ciangin and lai takin) (e:Huihpi a ~’ ciangin migilote len’mang a) (r:20.10.25/18.37.17) (q:draft)
paihkhiat = (t:v) (w:throw away/cast out/thrust out/forsake) (d:form of the verb used before words such as bangin, dongin, hun and thu) (e:Kep hun om a, ~ hun om hi) (r:21.3.6/12.17.20) (q:draft)
phaknatna = (t:n) (w:leprosy/skin disease) (d:a defiling disease of the skin) (e:a ~ bei-in a damsiang hi) (r:41.1.42/14.26.19) (q:draft)
phaknatna = (t:n) (w:mold/mildew) (d:a defiling growth on cloth or in a house) (e:puan khat peuhpeuh tungah ~ a om ciang) (r:3.13.47/3.14.55) (q:draft)
phasak = (t:v) (w:increase/multiply/make numerous) (e:mi tampi ka ~ ding hi) (b:pha) (r:38.10.8/1.17.2) (q:draft)
phasak = (t:v) (w:quench/satisfy) (d:satisfy thirst, as dangtakna phasak quench thirst; in one verse fill the year with bounty) (e:amah in a dangtakte ~ a) (b:pha) (r:19.107.9/16.9.20) (q:draft)
piazo = (t:v) (w:have given/grant) (d:pia give with zo marking the action as completed) (e:Topa in khuapi note hong ~ hi) (b:pia) (r:6.6.16/1.31.9) (q:draft)
pilte = (t:n) (w:the wise/wise ones) (d:plural of pil; after a noun it means wise, as numei pilte wise women) (e:A ~ ahih uh leh) (b:pil) (r:40.25.4/20.14.1) (q:draft)
puanung = (t:adj) (w:outer/outside) (d:the outer part, opposite of sungnung inner; tual puanung is the outer court) (e:biakinntual ~ ciang dongah kiza a) (r:26.10.5/11.6.30) (q:draft)
sawlpa = (t:n) (w:the one who sent/sender) (d:the man who sends, as kei hong sawlpa the one who sent me; pa marks a man) (e:Kei hong ~ zong a um hi) (b:sawl) (r:43.12.45/40.10.40) (q:draft)
sawlpa = (t:n) (w:the one sent/messenger) (d:the man whom someone sends, as ka sawlpa the one I send) (e:ka ~ a ngai mi in) (b:sawl) (r:43.13.20/43.6.29) (q:draft)
siahdongte = (t:n) (w:tax collectors/publicans) (e:~ leh migilote khempeuh in) (r:42.15.1/42.19.2) (q:draft)
siapa = (t:n) (w:teacher/master) (d:a male teacher, pa marks a man; thukham siapa is an expert in the law) (e:nungzuite in a ~ sangin lianzaw lo hi) (b:sia) (r:40.10.24/43.3.10) (q:draft)
siatsak = (t:v) (w:destroy/ruin/harm) (d:cause to be ruined) (e:an khempeuh a ~ ciangin) (b:siat) (r:19.105.16/5.8.20) (q:draft)
suanin = (t:v) (w:planting/plant) (d:suan plant with the linking suffix in, having planted) (e:Israel mual sang pen dawn-ah ~) (b:suan) (r:26.17.23) (q:draft)
suanin = (t:v) (w:rely/depend) (d:in the phrase suanin nei or muan le suanin nei, have as trust and support) (e:Pasian ~ nei un) (r:23.50.10/54.5.5) (q:draft, low confidence)
suanin = (t:v) (w:load/place on) (d:putting a load on the shoulder or on a pack animal) (e:liangko tungah naupang tawh ~ amah sawl khia) (r:1.21.14/16.13.15) (q:draft)
sumai = (t:v) (w:destroy/wipe out/put an end to) (e:mi khempeuh ka ~ ding hi) (r:36.1.4/28.1.5) (q:draft)
tawng = (t:n) (w:inmost part/depth/bottom) (d:the deepest or innermost part, as sung tawng the inmost being) (e:i sung ~ dong hong entel hi) (r:20.20.27) (q:draft)
tawng = (t:v) (w:threaten/intimidate/frighten) (e:sucip dingin mi ~ uh hi) (r:19.73.8/47.10.9) (q:draft)
thugennate = (t:n) (w:words/sayings/speeches) (e:ka ~ hong ngai in) (b:thugenna) (r:18.34.16/18.36.4) (q:draft)
tumna = (t:n) (w:setting/west) (d:the going down of the sun; ni tumna lam is the west side) (e:Ni ~ lam gamgi pen) (b:tum) (r:26.47.20/5.34.2) (q:draft)
tumna = (t:n) (w:entering/entrance/entry) (d:going in, as into a land, or the place of going in, as kongpi tumna the entrance of a gate) (e:luah dinga na ~ uh leitangah) (b:tum) (r:5.7.1/6.20.4) (q:draft)
tumna = (t:n) (w:blowing/blast) (d:the sounding of a trumpet or horn) (e:peengkul ~ tawh a kibawl phawkna) (b:tum) (r:3.23.24) (q:draft)
tuutalte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:rams) (e:tuuhonte' sung pan ~ ka ne kei hi) (b:tuutal) (r:1.31.38/26.39.18) (q:draft)
