taltang = (t:n) (w:forehead/brow) (e:amaute ~ tung uhah a om ding hi) (r:66.22.4/23.48.4) (q:draft)
tamna = (t:n) (w:abundance/great number/multitude) (d:tam, many, with na: the being many of something; sing tamna is a place of many trees) (e:Na mawhna a ~ hang) (b:tam) (r:18.22.5/14.27.4) (q:draft)
tanaute = (t:n) (w:relatives/kinsmen/clan) (d:tanau, relative, with the plural te; used also of one relative together with his family) (e:a nu’ ~ kiangah pai-in) (b:tanau) (r:7.9.1/8.2.1) (q:draft)
tauna = (t:n) (w:groaning/groan/moaning) (d:the sound made by one in pain or grief) (e:ka ~ in luipi ging bang ahi hi) (r:18.3.24/44.7.34) (q:draft)
