kisem = (t:v) (w:be done/be carried out/be performed) (d:sem work or do with ki-, passive) (e:thu a manin ~ ngei lo hi) (b:sem) (r:35.1.4/47.12.12) (q:draft)
kisem = (t:v) (w:be cut up/be cut in pieces) (d:in kisem nen, be cut into small pieces, said of a slaughtered animal) (e:Tuutal a ~ nen ciangin) (r:3.8.20) (q:draft, low confidence)
kivak = (t:v) (w:feed oneself/support oneself/live on) (d:provide food for oneself; with in or tawh after the food, live on it) (e:Kauphe leh gamlak khuaizu-in ~ hi) (r:41.1.6/3.25.35) (q:draft)
kivak = (t:v) (w:be lit/burn/shine) (d:vak light with ki-, passive: said of a lamp that is kept burning) (e:a tawntungin a ~ suak theih nadingin) (b:vak) (r:3.24.2/66.18.23) (q:draft)
kizopna = (t:n) (w:relationship/connection/fellowship/alliance) (d:a being joined together with others, by dealings, marriage or trade) (e:kuamah tawh ~ nei lo uh hi) (r:7.18.28/14.18.1) (q:draft)
kongpuankhai = (t:n) (w:curtain/hanging/door curtain) (d:cloth hung at an entrance: kong door, puan cloth, khai hang) (e:biakbuk kongkhak ding ~ a mun-ah khai hi) (r:2.40.28/2.40.8) (q:draft)
lakin = (t:v) (w:showing/pointing out) (d:lak show with the linking ending -in: showing, and so; used of showing a thing to someone and of making a matter known) (e:a an top teng a teeknu ~) (b:lak) (r:8.2.18/19.32.8) (q:draft)
lamlahna = (t:n) (w:guidance/direction/counsel) (d:a showing of the way: lam way, lah show, with -na; Topa tung panin lamlahna dong is to inquire of the Lord) (e:Topa tung panin ~ dong lo uh hi) (r:6.9.14/18.23.11) (q:draft)
lungduaina = (t:n) (w:patience/forbearance/longsuffering) (e:kiphatsakna sangin ~ hoihzaw hi) (b:lungduai) (r:21.7.8/48.5.22) (q:draft)
lunggulhna = (t:n) (w:longing/desire/lust) (d:strong desire, good or bad) (e:Ama ~ in kai a) (b:lunggulh) (r:59.1.14/10.23.15) (q:draft)
lungmuangin = (t:adv) (w:securely/safely/confidently) (d:with a mind at rest, without fear: lungmuang with the adverb ending -in) (e:thuman mite ~ om tawntung uh hi) (b:lungmuang) (r:20.10.25/20.18.10) (q:draft)
lungmuanna = (t:n) (w:security/safety/confidence/peace of mind) (e:Topa a zahtak mi in ~ nei a) (r:20.14.26/23.39.8) (q:draft)
lungngaingai = (t:v) (w:meditate/ponder/reflect on) (d:keep thinking something over; the doubled ngai shows continued action) (e:Nangma thuciamna a ~ dingin) (r:19.119.148/19.145.5) (q:draft)
makpa = (t:n) (w:son-in-law) (d:a man related by marriage through a daughter or kinswoman; -pa marks a man) (e:Horonaim khuami Sanballat’ ~ na hi hi) (b:mak) (r:16.13.28/9.18.26) (q:draft)
manunah = (t:conj) (w:because/since) (d:placed after a clause whose subject is plural: because they; also for fear that, after lau or kihtak) (e:a up loh ~ a tum zawh loh) (b:manun) (r:58.3.19/43.7.13) (q:draft)
meiite = (t:n) (w:clouds) (e:~ in leitungah guahzu sak hi) (b:meii) (r:20.3.20/20.8.28) (q:draft)
migi = (t:adj) (w:kind/good/gracious) (d:said of a person of good and gentle character; in Matthew 5:48 it stands for perfect) (e:~ tuucing ka hi hi) (r:43.10.14/56.2.5) (q:draft)
mipha = (t:n) (w:good person/the good/righteous person) (d:mi person with pha good; the opposite of misia) (e:~ in phatna thaman ngah hi) (r:20.14.14/42.1.6) (q:draft)
molhtum = (t:n) (w:club/rod/cudgel) (d:a heavy stick used as a weapon or for beating) (e:namsau leh ~ tawi-in na hong pai uh) (r:41.14.48/2.21.20) (q:draft)
nesak = (t:v) (w:make eat/feed/let eat) (d:ne eat with sak, cause or allow) (e:an kha a hong ~ hi) (b:ne) (r:25.3.15/24.19.9) (q:draft)
nete = (t:n) (w:eaters/those who eat) (d:ne eat or drink with -te, the ones who do so, usually after a; zu ne nete are those who keep drinking wine) (e:keimah hong ~ in kei hangin a nungta ding) (b:ne) (r:43.6.57/20.23.20) (q:draft)
ngeilo = (t:adv) (w:never) (d:placed after a verb: has never done or has never been so; ngei ever with lo not) (e:hih bang om ~ ahih manin) (b:ngei) (r:14.30.26/42.23.29) (q:draft)
niamkhiat = (t:v) (w:bring low/humble/abase) (d:make a proud person or place low) (e:Pasian in mi kiphasakte ~ a) (b:niam) (r:18.22.29/23.26.5) (q:draft)
nihveina = (t:num) (w:second time/second) (d:the second occasion of doing something: nihvei twice with -na) (e:Israel mite a ~ vun at kik in) (b:nihvei) (r:6.5.2/40.26.42) (q:draft)
nolh = (t:v) (w:reject/refuse/turn away) (d:refuse to accept or welcome a person or thing) (e:khua mite in no hong ~ leh) (r:42.10.10/5.32.19) (q:draft)
paisakin = (t:v) (w:sending/letting go) (d:paisak send or let go with the linking ending -in: sending, and so; hong paisakin is letting me go) (e:Efesa khua-ah mi ~ pawlpi upate a sam) (b:paisak) (r:44.20.17/9.20.29) (q:draft)
pawikhamna = (t:n) (w:feast/festival/celebration) (d:the keeping of a feast; Paisan pawikhamna is the Festival of the Passover) (e:~ sungah Pasian bia dinga hong paite) (b:pawikham) (r:43.12.20/42.2.41) (q:draft)
phuhsa = (t:adj) (w:founded/established/set up) (d:phuh set up or found with -sa, already done; ama phuhsa is which he has founded) (e:Mual siangtho tungah ama ~ khuapi om hi) (b:phuh) (r:19.87.1/20.22.28) (q:draft)
pulh = (t:v) (w:fall off/drop/shed) (d:come off and fall, said of flowers, leaves, unripe fruit and hair) (e:Lopa vul a, paak ~ hi) (r:23.40.8/3.13.40) (q:draft)
simsak = (t:v) (w:read to/read for) (d:sim read with sak: read something for another person, or have it read) (e:tua lai kigelh kong ~ ding a) (b:sim) (r:27.5.17/52.5.27) (q:draft)
simsak = (t:v) (w:let attack/send to attack) (d:sim attack with sak, cause or allow) (e:Israelte hong paikhiat lai-in na ~ loh) (b:sim) (r:14.20.10/26.28.7) (q:draft)
simsak = (t:v) (w:regard as/treat as) (d:in thupi simsak lo, not treat as serious) (e:thuaknate thupi ~ lo uh a) (b:sim) (r:24.8.11) (q:draft, low confidence)
sinso = (t:v) (w:be angry/burn with anger) (d:literally the liver is hot: sin liver with so hot; sinso-na is anger, wrath) (e:~ kawmin ka kiciam hi) (r:19.95.11/19.80.4) (q:draft)
sitbang = (t:adj) (w:blemished/defective/flawed) (d:having a fault, said of an animal for offering; a sitbang lo is without defect) (e:a ~ lo keel pa khat paipih ding a) (r:3.4.23/3.22.25) (q:draft)
suksiatsak = (t:v) (w:frustrate/thwart/destroy/bring to ruin) (d:suksiat destroy with sak; said of plans and schemes as well as things) (e:amah in migilote’ vaihawmna ~ hi) (b:suksiat) (r:19.146.9/28.10.2) (q:draft)
sungpan = (t:prep) (w:out of/from within) (d:sung inside with pan from; kam sungpan is out of the mouth) (e:nang ka kam ~ ka hong siakhia ding hi) (r:66.3.16/66.1.16) (q:draft)
susiamang = (t:v) (w:destroy completely/wipe out/annihilate) (d:susia destroy with mang, until gone) (e:Amalekte ka ~ khin hi) (r:9.15.20/7.1.17) (q:draft)
taangsak = (t:v) (w:make shine/cause to shine) (d:taang shine with the causative sak; mai taangsak is to make the face shine on someone, to show favour) (e:Na nasempa tungah na mai ~ in) (b:taang) (r:19.31.16/4.6.25) (q:draft)
tawmna = (t:n) (d:noun ending -na on a verb followed by tawm, doing something to oneself; in the verses only in kikhih tawmna, a pledge by which a woman binds herself, an obligation) (e:a kikhih ~ peuhmah ama tungah kip ding) (b:tawm) (r:4.30.9/4.30.7) (q:draft, low confidence)
tomkha = (t:n) (w:short while/little while/moment) (d:usually as tomkha sung, for a short time; also of a short distance, as in tomkha pai, go a little farther) (e:a kiang panin ~ sung a paikhia hi) (r:42.4.13/41.14.35) (q:draft)
tutphah = (t:n) (w:saddle/seat/stool/cushion) (d:something laid or set to sit on: tut sit with phah spread; la tutphah is a donkey's saddle, nausuahna tutphah the delivery stool) (e:kalaoh ~ sungah koihin) (r:1.31.34/4.22.21) (q:draft)
uiphukte = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:frogs) (e:huang sung leh lote panin ~ si hi) (r:2.8.13/19.78.45) (q:draft)
vankhainate = (t:n) (w:hooks/clasps) (d:plural of vankhaina, a thing on which something is hung or fastened, as the hooks and clasps of the tabernacle) (e:a ~ leh a gaknate in ngun) (r:2.38.10/2.35.11) (q:draft)
zuat = (t:v) (w:go to/head for/return to) (d:make one's way toward a place or person; the form used in dependent clauses and before nading) (e:tuikhuk a ~ uh leh tui) (r:24.14.3/20.26.11) (q:draft)
beeng = (t:v) (w:slap/hit/strike) (d:strike with the open hand, especially on the face) (e:ci-in khut tawh a ~ uh hi) (r:43.19.3/42.22.64) (q:draft)
beeng = (t:v) (w:clap) (d:with khut, hand: clap the hands) (e:na khut uh ~ un) (r:19.47.1) (q:draft)
buhtu = (t:n) (w:straw/stubble) (d:dry stalks of grain, used as fodder and in brick making) (e:mangbuhham leh ~ zong paipih uh hi) (r:11.4.28/2.5.12) (q:draft)
bulhin = (t:v) (w:putting on/fastening on/fitting) (d:bulh, put or fasten something on, with the connective in that links it to the next action) (e:amah kol ~ thong sungah koih hi) (b:bulh) (r:14.16.10/3.8.8) (q:draft)
bupa = (t:n) (w:captain/centurion/officer) (d:commander of a unit of men, pa marks a man; galkap bupa is a centurion) (e:galkap ~ kiangah a vaikhak hi) (r:44.24.23/23.3.3) (q:draft)
cihmawhna = (t:n) (w:distress/need/scarcity/hardship) (d:state of being helpless and in want) (e:amaute’ ~ a don hi) (r:19.106.44/20.6.11) (q:draft)
ciing = (t:adj) (w:barren/childless) (d:unable to bear children) (e:ahih hangin Rachel ~ hi) (r:1.29.31/1.11.30) (q:draft)
delhna = (t:n) (w:pursuit/pursuing/chasing) (d:act of chasing after someone; a delhna panin means from pursuing) (e:Abner a ~ panin Joab ciahkik hi) (b:delh) (r:10.2.30/19.35.6) (q:draft)
eng = (t:v) (w:envy/be envious of) (e:Migilote ~ kei in la) (r:20.24.1/19.73.3) (q:draft)
eng = (t:adj) (w:yellow) (e:siampipa in mul ~ a zon’ ding) (r:3.13.36) (q:draft)
ento = (t:v) (w:look up/look upward/look to) (d:en, look, with to, upward; also look to someone expectantly) (e:nangmah kong ~ hi) (b:en) (r:19.123.1/41.7.34) (q:draft)
galsimna = (t:n) (w:raid/battle/war/campaign) (d:act or occasion of going out to fight) (e:Siria mite in a ~ khat uhah) (b:galsim) (r:12.5.2/19.55.18) (q:draft)
gamsunga = (t:adv) (w:in the land/in the country) (d:gamsung, the inside of a land, with the ending a that links it to the words that follow: in the land of, that is in the land) (e:Izipt ~ a om kum sagih) (b:gamsung) (r:1.41.53/1.36.31) (q:draft)
gennop = (t:v) (w:want to say/mean) (d:gen, say, with nop, wish; gennop thu is what someone wants to say or means) (e:keima ngaihsutna ka ~ thu in) (r:46.7.12/43.10.6) (q:draft)
genthei = (t:adj) (w:distressed/afflicted/miserable/poor) (d:suffering hardship or anguish, often paired with cimawh, needy) (e:~ ka hih manin kei hong hehpih) (r:19.31.9/19.109.22) (q:draft)
genthei = (t:v) (w:can tell/be able to say) (d:gen, tell, with thei, be able) (e:nang kiangah hong ~ ding uh hi) (b:gen) (r:9.25.8) (q:draft)
hamtang = (t:adv) (w:deliberately/wilfully/insistently) (d:placed after a verb, shows that the action is done on purpose or with determination) (e:mualtung gamah na kuanto ~ uh hi) (r:5.1.43/28.5.11) (q:draft)
hamtang = (t:adv) (w:surely/without fail) (d:placed after a verb, shows that the event is certain to happen) (e:Migilote in daan a thuak ~ nading) (r:20.11.21/28.6.3) (q:draft)
hehpihhuai = (t:adj) (w:pitiable/pitiful/wretched) (d:deserving pity; hehpihhuai sa means feel compassion for) (e:mihonpite a muh ciangin ~ a sa hi) (r:40.9.36/1.41.19) (q:draft)
hingte = (t:n) (w:the living/living ones) (d:hing, alive, with plural te; a hingte gam is the land of the living; also said of green, living plants) (e:A ~ gam sungah) (b:hing) (r:19.27.13/19.37.2) (q:draft)
hupa = (t:n) (w:protector/defender/shield) (d:one who shields or defends, pa marks a male person; used of God) (e:Pasian in kei hong ~ hi a) (r:19.7.10/19.68.5) (q:draft)
kahtohna = (t:n) (w:ascent/way up/pass) (d:place where a road climbs, a slope or mountain pass) (e:Heres ~ lam tawnin ciahkik hi) (r:7.8.13/24.48.5) (q:draft)
khawlna = (t:n) (w:rest/resting place/stopping place/harbour) (d:place or act of stopping to rest; teembaw khawlna is a harbour for ships) (e:Krete gam teembaw ~ mun hi a) (b:khawl) (r:44.27.12/20.26.2) (q:draft)
khemsa-in = (t:v) (w:being deceived/deceived) (d:khem, deceive, with sa, already done, and the connective in; after a possessor and before om kei un it means do not be deceived by) (e:Hezekiah’ ~ om kei un) (r:12.18.29/18.36.18) (q:draft)
kibawlna = (t:n) (w:doing/making/performing) (d:noun form of kibawl, be made or done: the act, place or means of something being done; pawi kibawlna inn is a house where a feast is held) (e:Pawi ~ innah na pai kei ding) (b:kibawl) (r:24.16.8/2.29.33) (q:draft)
kikhenthang = (t:v) (w:be scattered/be divided/split up) (d:separate from one another, of people dispersing or forming factions) (e:kithutuak loin a ~ kik uh hi) (r:43.10.19/42.1.51) (q:draft)
kikhumna = (t:n) (w:prison/place of confinement/den/custody) (d:place where a person or animal is shut in) (e:Satan in a ~ pan kikhahin) (b:kikhum) (r:66.20.7/27.6.19) (q:draft)
kiksak = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb: cause to do or be again, from kik, again or back, with causative sak; nungta kiksak is bring back to life) (e:Pasian in a nungta ~ a) (b:kik) (r:44.13.30/19.90.3) (q:draft)
kimkota = (t:prep) (w:around/surrounding) (d:kimkot, around, with the ending a that links it to the following noun: that which is around) (e:Jerusalem khua ~ kulh khempeuh a susia hi) (b:kimkot) (r:24.52.14/26.41.12) (q:draft)
kinga = (t:v) (w:rest on/be set on/come to rest) (d:be placed so as to rest or lean on something) (e:Ararat mual tungah teembaw ~ hi) (r:1.8.4/14.4.4) (q:draft)
kinial = (t:v) (w:argue/dispute/contend) (d:argue with one another, tawh marks the other party) (e:Pasian tawh hih thu ka ~ nuam hi) (b:nial) (r:18.13.3/50.2.14) (q:draft)
kinial = (t:v) (w:be denied/be disowned) (d:passive of nial, deny) (e:Pasian’ vantungmite mai-ah ~ ding hi) (b:nial) (r:42.12.9) (q:draft)
kipuah = (t:v) (w:be polished/be put in order/be made ready) (d:passive of puah: be repaired, tidied or prepared for use) (e:Tua namsau limtakin ~ a) (b:puah) (r:26.21.11/42.11.25) (q:draft)
kitengkhia = (t:adj) (w:chosen/select/picked/best) (d:picked out from the rest, said of the best troops, chariots or officers) (e:a ~ leeng za guk leh Izipt) (r:2.14.7/14.13.17) (q:draft)
leiseek = (t:n) (w:brick) (d:block of moulded clay for building) (e:suang taangin ~ nei uh a) (r:1.11.3/2.5.7) (q:draft)
lenkip = (t:v) (w:hold fast/hold firmly/cling to) (d:len, hold, with kip, firm) (e:hih thu a ~ mihingte) (r:23.56.2/21.7.18) (q:draft)
let = (t:v) (w:overflow/flood) (d:of water, rise and spill over) (e:a ~ khia-in hong luang ding hi) (r:24.47.2/18.6.15) (q:draft)
let = (t:v) (w:hold/hold back/keep) (d:form of len, hold, used in dependent clauses) (e:amaute na ~ lai leh) (r:2.9.2) (q:draft)
let = (t:adv) (w:through/right through) (d:placed after a verb of stabbing or shooting: so that the weapon passes through the body) (e:tua tawh hong dawt ~ in) (r:9.31.4/4.24.8) (q:draft, low confidence)
luangte = (t:n) (w:bodies/corpses) (d:luang, dead body, with plural te) (e:mite in tua a ~ vuisak loin) (r:66.11.9/66.11.8) (q:draft)
luangte = (t:adj) (w:flowing/running) (d:luang, flow, with plural te: those that flow, said of streams and rivers) (e:guntui ~ na kangsak hi) (b:luang) (r:19.74.15/22.4.15) (q:draft)
lunghihmawh = (t:v) (w:worry/be anxious/be afraid) (d:be troubled in mind about what may happen) (e:nang na ~ nading om lo ding hi) (r:20.3.25/40.6.27) (q:draft)
munkip = (t:n) (w:fortress/stronghold/refuge) (d:literally firm place, a secure place of safety) (e:thuakte’ adingin ~ hi a) (r:19.9.9/19.91.2) (q:draft)
ngiate = (t:n) (c:animal) (w:jackals/foxes/wolves) (d:plural of ngia, a wild animal of the dog kind; the verses use it for jackal, fox and wolf) (e:inn sia lak-a om ~ tawh kibang) (r:26.13.4/7.15.5) (q:draft)
nuamsak = (t:v) (w:gladden/cheer/make happy) (d:nuam, glad, with causative sak; lung nuamsak is gladden the heart) (e:zu in lung ~ a) (b:nuam) (r:21.10.19/11.21.7) (q:draft)
nungdelh = (t:v) (w:pursue/chase after/run after) (d:nung, behind, with delh, chase) (e:Assiria mite na ~ lai hi) (r:26.16.28/25.3.43) (q:draft)
paikhiasak = (t:v) (w:send away/let go/make go out) (d:paikhia, go out, with causative sak) (e:khut guak tawh a ~ zo hi) (b:paikhia) (r:42.1.53/42.14.4) (q:draft)
pei = (t:n) (w:wheel) (d:wheel of a cart or chariot, as in leengpei) (e:lamin ~ khat ciat nei thuah uh) (r:26.1.16/26.10.12) (q:draft)
pei = (t:v) (w:shake/wag) (d:with lu, head: shake the head from side to side, in mockery) (e:ka lu hong ~ sanin) (r:18.16.4/41.15.30) (q:draft)
pekin = (t:adv) (w:long ago/long before/already) (d:pek with the adverb ending in; stresses how far back in time something was so, as in ma pekin, long before, and lai pekin, back when) (e:mualneute a kibawl ma ~ ka om khin hi) (b:pek) (r:20.8.25/44.15.7) (q:draft)
penpen = (t:part) (w:the very most) (d:doubled pen, most, placed after a descriptive word for a strong superlative: the very best, the worst ever) (e:Amah in leitang hoih ~ zong a) (r:20.31.16/27.12.1) (q:draft)
penpen = (t:part) (d:placed after a verb phrase: whichever one, the very one that) (e:nih lakah na teel ~ hong lak in) (r:44.1.25/1.44.10) (q:draft, low confidence)
peuhmahte = (t:pron) (w:whoever/all who/whatever) (d:plural of peuhmah, placed after a clause: all those who, any that) (e:kei hong zong ~ in hong mu uh hi) (b:peuhmah) (r:20.8.17/1.9.6) (q:draft)
piaksak = (t:v) (w:offer for/give on behalf of) (d:piak, give, with sak: give or offer something for another person, as a priest offers a sacrifice for someone) (e:amau’ adingin biakna ~ uh hi) (b:piak) (r:12.17.32/3.7.8) (q:draft)
piaksak = (t:v) (w:make give/have given) (d:piak, give, with causative sak: cause something to be given or handed over) (e:kikhamna sum a ~ khit uh ciangin) (b:piak) (r:44.17.9/7.15.6) (q:draft, low confidence)
piangkhia = (t:v) (w:come forth/arise/be born/break out) (d:piang, come into being, with khia, out: spring out of, originate from) (e:Amaute sungah mei hong ~ a) (b:piang) (r:19.106.18/23.48.1) (q:draft)
pingpei = (t:n) (w:whirlwind/windstorm) (e:Na vanging lianpi ~ sungah om-in) (r:19.77.18/12.2.1) (q:draft)
puantungsilh = (t:n) (w:tunic/coat/cloak/outer garment) (d:garment worn over the others, contrasted with puansungsilh, the inner garment) (e:na ~ zong na piathuah lai in) (r:40.5.40/2.29.8) (q:draft)
pukna = (t:n) (w:fall/downfall/defeat) (e:kiphatsakna in ~ hong piang sak hi) (b:puk) (r:20.16.18/19.92.11) (q:draft)
