leteh = (t:conj) (w:if/if only) (d:placed after a verb: if one does so, should one do so; also used in wishes and polite requests) (e:hong bia ~ hihte khempeuh nangma aa) (r:42.4.7/40.20.33) (q:draft)
limlang = (t:n) (w:mirror/glass/crystal) (d:a mirror, or clear glass) (e:tua pa in ~ ah ama maitang a en) (r:59.1.23/66.21.18) (q:draft)
lolai = (t:n) (w:field/open field) (d:lo field with lai middle: the cultivated field, the open field; lolai-ah is in the field) (e:~ pen leitung hi a) (r:40.13.38/41.13.16) (q:draft)
lungkhamin = (t:v) (w:be distressed/be in anguish/despair/grieve) (d:lungkham with the ending in, which links it to the following verb: being distressed, in anguish) (e:lunggim ~ si uh hi) (b:lungkham) (r:18.21.25/9.1.10) (q:draft)
maisakin = (t:v) (w:forgive/pardon/cancel) (d:maisak with the ending in, which links it to the following verb: forgiving a sin or cancelling a debt and then doing something more) (e:a leiba khempeuh ~ a khah hi) (b:maisak) (r:40.18.27/14.6.25) (q:draft)
mante = (t:n) (w:captors/catchers) (d:man catch, seize, with plural te: those who catch or hold captive; mi mante is catchers of people, fishers of men) (e:Mi ~ kong suaksak ding hi) (b:man) (r:41.1.17/11.8.47) (q:draft)
mante = (t:n) (w:prices/values) (d:man price, with plural te) (e:na keeltal ~ in lo cing khat) (b:man) (r:20.27.26) (q:draft, low confidence)
misiangtho = (t:n) (w:saint/holy one/holy people) (d:mi person with siangtho holy: a holy person, one of God's people; also said of the Holy One of God) (e:Pasian’ ~ na hi ci-in) (r:43.6.69/49.1.15) (q:draft)
muhtheih = (t:v) (w:be able to see/can see) (d:muh see with theih can, the form used before nading or a noun: muhtheih nadingin is so that one may see, i muhtheih nate is the things we can see, visible things) (e:a nai takin a ~ nadingin) (b:muh) (r:44.7.31/58.11.3) (q:draft)
naupangno = (t:n) (w:little child/small child/young child) (d:naupang child with no small, young) (e:hih ~ bang na suah kei uh leh) (b:naupang) (r:40.18.3/9.20.35) (q:draft)
nawt = (t:v) (w:gore/push/thrust) (d:push hard against something, as an ox with its horns; nawt gawp is treat roughly, assault) (e:hihte tawh Siria mite na ~ ding hi) (r:14.18.10/20.19.26) (q:draft)
nawt = (t:v) (w:press forward/advance/march on) (d:with mai face: mai nawt, push ahead, go forward) (e:Thakhauh takin mai ka ~ suak ding hi) (r:7.5.21) (q:draft)
nawt = (t:v) (w:wear away/rub off/wash away) (d:rub or scrape against a surface so that it wears off, usually with khia out) (e:guahtui in lei a ~ khiat bangin) (r:18.14.19) (q:draft, low confidence)
nikhat = (t:n) (w:one day/a day) (d:ni day with khat one; nikhat ni-in is on a certain day, nikhat sung lam is a day's journey) (e:~ sung lam a pai khit ciangin) (r:32.3.4/18.1.6) (q:draft)
nunglam = (t:n) (w:back/rear/behind) (d:nung back with lam side, direction: the back side, the direction behind; of a ship the stern; nunglam en is look back) (e:Nitumna lam biakbuk ~ adingin) (r:2.36.27/42.9.62) (q:draft)
omkhin = (t:v) (w:have already been/already exist) (d:om be with khin already, finished: have been somewhere or in a state up to now, was already there before) (e:ni thum bang hong ~ uh a) (b:om) (r:41.8.2/43.1.30) (q:draft)
paang = (t:n) (w:cheek/temple/jaw) (d:the side of the face or head: the cheek that is slapped, the temple; in Leviticus 13.41 used of the front part of the head from which hair is lost) (e:hong kai mite tungah ka ~ ka dawh hi) (r:23.50.6/7.4.21) (q:draft)
paikhiatpihna = (t:n) (w:bringing out/leading out) (d:noun from paikhiatpih: the act or fact of bringing or leading someone out; also the place or people to which one is led out) (e:Israel mite a ~ thu za hi) (b:paikhiatpih) (r:2.18.1/5.28.37) (q:draft)
peel = (t:v) (w:avoid/shun/keep away from/beware of) (d:stay clear of a person or thing, turn away from) (e:Gitlohna ~ in) (r:20.4.15/50.3.2) (q:draft)
peel = (t:v) (w:fail to keep/evade/break) (d:of a covenant or an appointed observance: evade it, not keep it; peel loin is without fail) (e:tawntung thuciamna ~ uh hi) (r:23.24.5/17.9.27) (q:draft, low confidence)
phate = (t:n) (w:those who have reached/those aged) (d:pha reach, amount to, with plural te: those who have reached a stated age or number) (e:kum sawmguk a ~ a man) (b:pha) (r:3.27.3/4.8.24) (q:draft)
phate = (t:n) (w:good ones/good things) (d:pha good with plural te: the good, what is good; gamtatna phate is good deeds) (e:A ~ sia ci-in) (b:pha) (r:23.5.20/40.5.16) (q:draft)
phuh = (t:v) (w:found/build/establish/set up) (d:form of phut used in dependent clauses and before endings: set up a post, lay a foundation, found a city) (e:a khuam a ~ khit ciangin) (r:42.14.29/5.6.10) (q:draft)
poina = (t:n) (w:defect/blemish/flaw) (d:noun from poi be hurt, damaged: a bodily defect or injury in a person or an animal) (e:a khangin ~ a nei mi in) (r:3.21.17/5.15.21) (q:draft)
puakkik = (t:v) (w:send back/bring back/return) (d:puak carry, send, with kik back, again) (e:kiangah kong ~ uh hi) (b:puak) (r:1.44.8/24.38.26) (q:draft)
puksi = (t:v) (w:perish/die of hunger/starve) (d:puk fall with si die: fall down dead; in the verses mostly of dying from hunger) (e:kial-in a ~ ding uh hi) (r:24.11.22/25.4.9) (q:draft)
siatnate = (t:n) (w:disasters/calamities/evils) (e:hih ~ i tungah hong tung) (b:siatna) (r:5.31.17) (q:draft)
siatnate = (t:n) (w:evil deeds/wickedness) (d:often after gamtat conduct: gamtat siatnate, evil doings) (e:na gamtat ~ uh paikhia un) (b:siatna) (r:23.1.16/30.8.7) (q:draft)
simah = (t:ppm) (w:on each/at each/from each/on every) (d:sim each, every, with the place marker ah; placed after the noun: tau simah on each altar, minam simah from each tribe) (e:biakna tau ~ bawngtal khat) (r:4.23.30/4.34.18) (q:draft, low confidence)
sungnungah = (t:n) (w:in the inner part/into the inner part/in the inner room) (d:sungnung inner, inner room, with the place marker ah: in or into the inner part; tual sungnungah is into the inner court, biakinn sungnungah in the inner sanctuary) (e:a tual ~ hong paipih a) (b:sungnung) (r:26.43.5/11.6.23) (q:draft)
taleng = (t:conj) (w:even if/even though/although) (d:placed after the verb and often followed by zong: even if, though it be so; alone it can also express a wish, if only) (e:tuipimong pek-ah om ~ zong) (r:19.139.9/19.69.11) (q:draft)
tawntunga = (t:adv) (w:always/forever/continually/throughout) (d:tawntung with the linking ending a, used before a verb or noun; a tawntunga kipan is from everlasting, khang tawntunga is throughout all generations) (e:a ~ thuman-a gamta mite in) (b:tawntung) (r:19.106.3/19.90.2) (q:draft)
tecite = (t:n) (w:witnesses) (e:zuau ~ in khemna thu bek gen) (b:teci) (r:20.12.17/19.35.11) (q:draft)
teengin = (t:v) (w:dwell/live/settle) (d:teeng with the ending in, which links it to the following verb: dwelling, living there and) (e:tua sungah ~ sum bawl un la) (b:teeng) (r:1.34.10/2.29.45) (q:draft)
teengsak = (t:v) (w:settle/cause to dwell/let live) (d:teeng with causative sak: make or allow someone to live in a place) (e:a pa leh a sanggamte ~ hi) (b:teeng) (r:1.47.11/24.7.7) (q:draft)
thanem = (t:adj) (w:weak/feeble) (d:tha strength with nem soft: having little strength) (e:Amah in ~ ahih ciangin) (r:58.5.2/23.16.14) (q:draft)
theipa = (t:n) (w:one who can/one who is able) (d:thei can, know how, with pa marking a man: the man who is able to, placed after a verb; with aw in address: mi khem theipa aw, you deceiver) (e:a lam kik ~ aw) (b:thei) (r:40.27.39/19.52.4) (q:draft)
theipa = (t:n) (w:one who knows/learned man) (d:thei know with pa marking a man: the man who knows; lai theipa, the man who knows writing, is the scribe or teacher of the Law) (e:lai ~ Ezra kiangah hong kikhawm uh hi) (b:thei) (r:16.8.13/19.45.1) (q:draft)
them = (t:n) (w:piece/bit/fragment/scrap) (d:a small broken piece or particle of something; them khat zong with a negative is not even a bit; them len is be dashed to pieces) (e:beel kitam ~ khat la-in) (r:18.2.8/14.25.12) (q:draft)
thupizaw = (t:adj) (w:greater/more important/better) (d:thupi with comparative zaw; the thing compared is marked by sangin, than) (e:pumpi pen puan sangin ~ hi) (b:thupi) (r:42.12.23/37.2.9) (q:draft)
umlebeel = (t:n) (w:articles/vessels/utensils/containers) (d:um gourd, le and, beel pot: household vessels and containers in general; in the verses the articles of the temple and storage vats) (e:~ a nam tuamtuam sawmnih le kua) (r:15.1.9/14.36.7) (q:draft)
vah = (t:v) (w:be full/be satisfied) (d:have eaten enough, usually with gil stomach: gil vah; vah sak is satisfy, feed until full) (e:na gil uh a ~ ciangin) (r:28.13.6/29.2.26) (q:draft)
valhtum = (t:v) (w:swallow/swallow up/devour) (d:valh swallow with tum go in: swallow whole) (e:lei kihongin Dathan ~ a) (r:19.106.17/23.49.19) (q:draft)
vanmanpha = (t:n) (w:treasure/valuables/precious things) (d:van goods with manpha precious; vanmanpha koihna is the treasury, the place where valuables are kept) (e:~ koihna ah kham darik) (r:16.7.71/13.26.22) (q:draft)
zahhuai = (t:v) (w:be put to shame/be ashamed/be disgraced) (d:zahhuai sak is put someone to shame) (e:Ka galte khempeuh ~ in genthei mahmah) (r:19.6.10/19.127.5) (q:draft)
zalin = (t:v) (w:spread out/stretch out) (d:zal with the ending in, which links it to the following verb: spreading, stretching out, said of wings and of the heavens) (e:Simbung in a kha ~ leitaw lamah) (b:zal) (r:18.39.26/38.12.1) (q:draft)
